        // The Lava Gun (0x303F88; effects.md, "Each gun's effects") [code]: its stream is
        // three ribbons through its points (0x305CA0) narrowing 0.94 a point, blended by
        // the GS's fixed alpha (FIX) rather than their own: a core (10) mixed at 0x40, a
        // band (14) added at 0x40 and a glow (43) six times as wide added at 0x50; two
        // glows (44) at the nozzle; and the stream sheds
        // smoke (0x6D) that darkens as it drifts and sparks (0x19) going from white to red
        // as they fall. Its smokes take turns at being added and blended (0x305710 [code],
        // 0x48 and 0x44 at 0x1DC610 [data]), each darkened by up to half. A point that
        // meets the world leaves a burning pool one time in 11, up to 10 (0x3063C8, drawn by
        // 0x306838): two glows of 11 lying on the surface and two flames of 23 standing on
        // it, one blended and one added, their texture scrolling up them; its strength
        // springs to full in 36 ticks, holds 60 and springs back, the flames growing with
        // it and everything fading with it. From V5, only the glows, in blue.
